Aw.

1295
00:55:01.450 --> 00:55:03.050
But they're pros, everybody.

1296
00:55:03.430 --> 00:55:04.110
They're lovely.

1297
00:55:04.590 --> 00:55:11.990
I feel like I can reveal this one thing because I found it really charming, which is that we also got to tour the writer's space.

1298
00:55:12.130 --> 00:55:12.450
Yes.

1299
00:55:12.450 --> 00:55:20.690
Which was really neat when I went into the writer's room and they had all the cards on the board, just like we had cards on the board.

1300
00:55:20.870 --> 00:55:31.990
But then I looked over at the episode that you were shooting and there were three photographs from the office and they were shots of us in cars driving.

1301
00:55:32.830 --> 00:55:45.990
And I asked about it and Kelly said, oh, yeah, that's because we have some driving shots coming up and we were just looking at for research, how do you shoot in a car?

1302
00:55:46.270 --> 00:55:46.470
Yeah.

1303
00:55:46.630 --> 00:55:49.510
And Greg was saying the lipstick cameras and you.

1304
00:55:49.670 --> 00:55:51.190
I'm the one who provided the pictures.

1305
00:55:51.530 --> 00:55:52.950
Oh, of course.

1306
00:55:53.230 --> 00:55:54.070
And I was, yeah.

1307
00:55:54.310 --> 00:55:55.890
I took a picture of them.

1308
00:55:56.070 --> 00:55:56.690
I did too.

1309
00:55:57.070 --> 00:55:57.970
I was there.

1310
00:55:58.370 --> 00:55:59.430
I was in one of them.

1311
00:55:59.630 --> 00:55:59.770
Yeah.

1312
00:56:00.190 --> 00:56:01.650
Well, yeah, because we should.

1313
00:56:01.810 --> 00:56:04.850
I think yours was probably Andy's Ancestry.

1314
00:56:05.130 --> 00:56:05.370
Yes.

1315
00:56:05.370 --> 00:56:06.690
It was me and Nellie.

1316
00:56:06.750 --> 00:56:07.290
You and Nellie.

1317
00:56:07.410 --> 00:56:08.350
And I had directed that one.

1318
00:56:08.450 --> 00:56:09.250
So I had that one.

1319
00:56:09.370 --> 00:56:11.590
And there was one of Michael and Daryl.

1320
00:56:12.010 --> 00:56:12.310
Yeah.

1321
00:56:12.350 --> 00:56:13.230
And that was another one I did.

1322
00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:14.590
That was an employee transfer.

1323
00:56:15.510 --> 00:56:20.270
Those were ones I directed because I had, I remember just struggling, like, how are we going to do the camera angles?

1324
00:56:20.370 --> 00:56:21.930
Like, what do we, you know, because you have to choose.

1325
00:56:22.150 --> 00:56:27.430
You don't, you know, when you're shooting an interior car scene and you have the, what we call the lipstick caMs.

1326
00:56:27.570 --> 00:56:27.690
Right.

1327
00:56:27.770 --> 00:56:29.490
You can only get so many cameras in there.

1328
00:56:29.490 --> 00:56:29.950
Yep, right.

1329
00:56:30.070 --> 00:56:32.150
So it's like, do you want the, you know, a raking shot?

1330
00:56:32.290 --> 00:56:33.070
Do you want a single?

1331
00:56:33.270 --> 00:56:38.930
What, you know, so this, we were just looking at these kinds of frames and to say, like, hey, this is, you know, what we're going for.

1332
00:56:39.070 --> 00:56:44.490
And I had a conversation with the DP afterwards because she wanted to show, like, the camera.

1333
00:56:44.630 --> 00:56:47.570
She's like, well, we should see the cameras, you know, when we're outside the car.

1334
00:56:47.670 --> 00:56:48.090
I'm like, nope.

1335
00:56:48.570 --> 00:56:53.030
I'm like, whenever we did this on the show, we would not, that's the precedent.

1336
00:56:53.030 --> 00:56:59.870
Whatever we, you know, we would have these lipstick cams, but sometimes we would have, you know, we would go film the actual car and you wouldn't see them.

1337
00:56:59.950 --> 00:57:01.370
We didn't want to obscure the actors' faces.

1338
00:57:01.430 --> 00:57:05.510
We just buy that these are very, very tiny cameras that are in there.

1339
00:57:05.510 --> 00:57:06.750
That's such a good point.

1340
00:57:07.010 --> 00:57:16.230
So this is so interesting then because you are now on the paper preserving the look of the office because it's the documentary crew.

1341
00:57:16.410 --> 00:57:17.630
It's the same documentary crew.

1342
00:57:17.650 --> 00:57:19.790
So they will have shot it the same way.

1343
00:57:19.990 --> 00:57:22.510
There's still some new things that they can do.

1344
00:57:22.530 --> 00:57:27.810
But, yes, there are certain things that, you know, like this is the point is that it exists in this universe.

1345
00:57:27.970 --> 00:57:31.390
We're not doing like a – I mean there are so many mockumentary shows out there right now.

1346
00:57:31.390 --> 00:57:38.910
And, you know, that's one thing I'll say, Greg, you know, he kind of wanted to get back to basics with, you know, the style of the office.

1347
00:57:38.950 --> 00:57:43.010
And like I don't want to have – feel like there's 15 cameras around, you know.

1348
00:57:43.170 --> 00:57:43.390
Yeah, right.

1349
00:57:44.030 --> 00:57:55.630
And so, you know, and there have been a lot of, I think, important creative decisions on just, you know, everything from the casting to the set to the, you know,

1350
00:57:55.770 --> 00:57:57.850
style of the show and what we're doing.

1351
00:57:58.430 --> 00:57:59.190
So, yeah.

1352
00:57:59.250 --> 00:58:00.330
Well, we're excited.

1353
00:58:00.410 --> 00:58:01.530
We're excited to see it.

1354
00:58:01.650 --> 00:58:01.700
Yeah.

1355
00:58:02.070 --> 00:58:04.390
Last question for you, Dave, before you leave.

1356
